        <p><strong>How does the restaurant POS handle table management and kitchen orders?</strong> The restaurant module includes table/floor management, kitchen display or KOT printing, menu and recipe-based inventory deduction, and support for dine-in, takeaway, and delivery order types. It’s built to handle the fast pace of restaurant operations without slowing down service.</p>
        <p><strong>Can the gold shop module handle karat-based and weight-based pricing?</strong> Yes, our gold shop solution supports pricing based on weight, karat, and live or manually updated gold rates, along with making charges and stone value calculations. This ensures accurate, transparent pricing for every transaction in a market where rates fluctuate daily.</p>
        <p><strong>Does MultiTech POS support appointment booking for salons?</strong> Yes, the salon module includes appointment scheduling, stylist/staff assignment, service-based billing, and inventory tracking for products used during services. This helps salons manage both walk-in and pre-booked clients efficiently.</p>
        <p><strong>Can the tailor shop module track custom orders and measurements?</strong> Yes, our tailoring solution allows you to record customer measurements, track custom order status from intake to delivery, and manage advance payments and balances per order. This is especially useful for businesses juggling multiple custom orders simultaneously.</p>
        <p><strong>How does the distribution/van sales module work?</strong> Our distribution and van sales features support route-based selling, real-time stock tracking for mobile sales teams, and synchronization between van inventory and your central warehouse. Sales reps can process orders and payments on the go, with data syncing back to your main system.</p>
        <p><strong>Does the system support multi-branch fashion or bike shop retail operations?</strong> Yes, MultiTech POS supports multi-branch inventory visibility, transfers between branches, and consolidated reporting, which is essential for fashion retailers and bike shops managing stock across several locations or seasonal product lines.</p>
        <h2><strong>Inventory &amp; Stock Management</strong></h2>
        <p><strong>Can MultiTech POS track stock across multiple branches?</strong> Yes, the system provides centralized inventory visibility across all your branches, with the ability to transfer stock between locations and generate branch-level or consolidated stock reports. This helps prevent overselling and gives you a clear picture of inventory wherever it sits.</p>
        <p><strong>Does it alert me when stock is running low?</strong> Yes, you can set minimum stock thresholds per product, and the system will alert you when inventory falls below that level so you can reorder before running out. This is particularly useful for fast-moving items in pharmacy, gift store, and distribution businesses.</p>
        <p><strong>Can I manage suppliers and purchase orders within the system?</strong> Yes, MultiTech POS includes supplier management, purchase order creation, and goods receiving, so your entire procurement cycle is tracked alongside your sales data in one place.</p>
        <h2><strong>Employee Management &amp; Reporting</strong></h2>
        <p><strong>Does MultiTech POS include employee management features?</strong> Yes, the system includes staff login with role-based permissions, attendance tracking, sales performance by employee, and commission tracking where applicable (such as for salon stylists or sales reps). This gives you visibility into staff productivity without needing a separate HR tool.</p>
        <p><strong>What kind of reports can I generate?</strong> You can generate sales reports, inventory reports, profit and loss summaries, employee performance reports, and branch comparison reports. Reports can typically be filtered by date range, branch, product category, or staff member to give you the specific insight you need.</p>
        <p><strong>Can different staff have different access levels?</strong> Yes, you can assign role-based permissions so cashiers, managers, and admin staff only see and access the features relevant to their role. This protects sensitive data like cost prices, profit margins, and financial reports from unauthorized access.</p>
